# PyTorch Standards

Whenever you write or modify PyTorch matrix operations, conv layers, pooling, linear layers, or reshapes, **always comment the expected input and output tensor shapes** directly above the operation.

## Format

Use inline shape comments in bracket notation:

```python
# in: [batch_size, in_channels, height, width]
# out: [batch_size, out_channels, height//2, width//2]
x = self.conv1(x)
x = F.relu(x)
x = self.pool(x)

# in: [batch_size, flattened_features]
# out: [batch_size, num_classes]
logits = self.fc(x)
```

## Apply To

- `nn.Conv2d`, `nn.Linear`, `nn.BatchNorm*`, pooling, attention, matmul, `view`/`reshape`, `permute`, `cat`, `stack`
- Any operation where shape changes are non-obvious

## Do Not Skip

Even for simple ops, include shapes when dimensions change. Omit comments only for trivial in-place ops (e.g., `F.relu`) where input and output shapes are identical.
